WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.120
In the early Wanli years, the young Emperor Wanli was still a child, so Zhang Juzheng directed the court and diligently managed the affairs of state.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:16.440
Zhang Juzheng reformed the conduct of officials, requiring them to work diligently and forbidding laziness, corruption, and waste.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.480
Officials held thick registers and lined up to be inspected.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:27.480
He ordered a survey of land across the country, uncovered hidden farmland, and made taxation fairer.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:32.440
The surveyors traveled through the fields and recorded every plot of land clearly.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:38.720
He reformed the tax and labor-service system, combined many miscellaneous taxes, and eased the people's heavy burden.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:45.640
The reforms gradually filled the state treasury, and the court's finances and administrative efficiency clearly improved.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:50.520
The storehouses were piled full of grain, and officials were busy counting the amounts.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:56.640
Although the reforms caused great controversy, they are a very important event for understanding Ming dynasty politics.
